From c174777c8a9001d38909759493f8febd4e722461 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtio-gpu-desktop <local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] virtio-gpu-rutabaga: do not leak the scanout image of a
 freed resource

rutabaga_cmd_set_scanout() creates res->image (one reference) and then takes a second one that
nothing ever drops: the display surface takes and drops its own (qemu_create_displaysurface_pixman /
the surface replacement), and the resource's unref drops one. So every resource that was ever shown
leaves its image behind: width * height * 4 bytes (4 MB at 1280x800) per freed scanout buffer.

Measured 2026-10-14 on the desktop (RX 6900 XT, nested guest, bench/ab/scanout_leak_ab_1014.sh lk1):
the fork's QEMU grows 4,000 KiB per scanout cycle (rounds of 10/20/50: +35/+78/+195 MiB), with this
change 0 (209.4 MiB flat). Under ASan (qemu_leaktest_run_1012.sh, SCANOUT_CHURN=50, REBOOT=1): the
fork reports "Indirect leak of 192512000 byte(s) in 47 object(s)" from rutabaga_cmd_set_scanout,
this change none from there, and no ASan error (no use-after-free) over the churn, a guest reboot
(device reset) and shutdown. The image is created with NULL data (pixman owns its buffer), so no
memory depends on the extra reference.

Local fix of the fork (the user: "start with a fix, to send it upstream we'll see"); not submitted.
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-rutabaga.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-rutabaga.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-rutabaga.c
index f49260a37a..fc67bfc759 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-rutabaga.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-rutabaga.c
@@ -388,7 +388,6 @@ rutabaga_cmd_set_scanout(VirtIOGPU *g, struct virtio_gpu_ctrl_command *cmd)
                                               res->height,
                                               NULL, 0);
         CHECK(res->image, cmd);
-        pixman_image_ref(res->image);
     }
 
     vb->enable = 1;
